# NOBORU UI/UX RULE

Version: 1.0

Priority: CRITICAL

Status: AUTHORITATIVE

This rule governs all user interface and user experience decisions within Noboru.

Every screen, interaction, animation, component, page, dialog, onboarding flow, game, lesson, and notification must follow this document.

This document is considered the primary source of truth for user experience.

⸻

PURPOSE

Noboru must feel:

Premium

Calm

Focused

Modern

Motivating

Adventure-Oriented

Educational

The experience should encourage users to continue climbing.

The experience should never feel overwhelming.

⸻

UX PHILOSOPHY

Users are climbers.

Not customers.

Not students.

Not productivity machines.

Everything should reinforce progress and discovery.

⸻

PRIMARY EXPERIENCE GOAL

The user should consistently feel:

“I am getting better.”

Not:

“I am checking boxes.”

Not:

“I am maintaining a streak.”

Not:

“I am completing chores.”

⸻

CORE FEELING

Noboru should feel like:

A mountain expedition through Japan.

Combined with:

Apple-level polish

Nintendo-level charm

Modern mobile usability

Premium educational quality

⸻

VISUAL PILLARS

Clarity

Users should instantly understand what to do.

⸻

Focus

One primary action per screen.

⸻

Progress

Progress should always be visible.

⸻

Delight

Small moments of satisfaction.

Never distraction.

⸻

Consistency

Every screen should feel like Noboru.

⸻

MOBILE FIRST RULE

All experiences must be designed for mobile first.

Desktop adapts from mobile.

Never the reverse.

⸻

THUMB REACHABILITY

Primary actions must remain reachable.

Critical actions belong:

Bottom area

Bottom sheets

Bottom navigation

Floating actions when appropriate

⸻

SCREEN PRIORITY RULE

Every screen must answer:

Where am I?

What should I do?

Why does it matter?

What progress am I making?

Within 3 seconds.

⸻

NAVIGATION PRINCIPLES

Navigation must be simple.

No deep nesting.

No confusing routes.

No hidden critical features.

⸻

PRIMARY NAVIGATION

Bottom Navigation:

Home

Learn

Review

Games

Community

Profile

Maximum:

6 primary items

⸻

NAVIGATION ITEM DEFINITIONS

Home

Dashboard entry point.

Shows daily quest, level progress, upcoming lesson, and quick actions.

Learn

Learning path, lessons, vocabulary, grammar, and kanji.

Review

Spaced repetition and review queue.

Games

Educational mini-games that reinforce mastery.

Community

Social features, challenges, and leagues.

Profile

User identity, stats, achievements, and account access.

⸻

HOME SCREEN RULE

The home screen must always show:

Current Region

Current Trail

Progress

Daily Goals

Continue Learning

Elevation Progress

Recent Achievements

⸻

DARK MODE RULE

Dark mode is primary.

Design dark mode first.

Then create light mode.

Not the reverse.

⸻

DARK MODE FEEL

Theme:

Mountain Night

Feeling:

Calm

Focused

Premium

Readable

Never harsh.

Never neon.

Never cyberpunk.

⸻

LIGHT MODE FEEL

Theme:

Mountain Dawn

Feeling:

Fresh

Clean

Elegant

Optimistic

⸻

COLOR PHILOSOPHY

Colors communicate meaning.

Never decoration.

⸻

PRIMARY BRAND COLOR

Mountain Red

Used for:

Primary Actions

Progress

Elevation

Important Highlights

⸻

SUCCESS COLOR

Used only for:

Completion

Achievements

Positive Reinforcement

⸻

WARNING COLOR

Used only for:

Important Warnings

Learning Risks

Critical Notices

